    <exercise number="1" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <list type="ordered">
          <item>What is an alternating series?</item>
          <item>Under what conditions does an alternating series converge?</item>
          <item>If these conditions are satisfied, what can you say about the remainder after $$n$$ terms?</item>
        </list>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>A series whose terms are alternately positive and negative</paragraph>
        <paragraph>$$0 &lt; b_{n + 1} \leqslant b_{n}$$ and $$\lim_{n^{}\rightarrow\infty}b_{n} = 0$$ , where $$b_{n} = \left| a_{n} \right|$$</paragraph>
        <paragraph>$$\left| R_{n} \right| \leqslant b_{n + 1}$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
