    <exercise number="21" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <list type="ordered">
          <item>What does it mean for a series to be absolutely convergent?</item>
          <item>What does it mean for a series to be conditionally convergent?</item>
          <item>If the series of positive terms $$\sum_{n = 1}^{\infty}b_{n}$$ converges, then what can you say about the series $$\sum_{n = 1}^{\infty}( - 1)^{n}b_{n}$$ ?</item>
        </list>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>The series $$\sum a_{n}$$ is absolutely convergent if $$\left. \sum \middle| a_{n} \right|$$ converges.</paragraph>
        <paragraph>The series $$\sum a_{n}$$ is conditionally convergent if $$\sum a_{n}$$ converges but $$\left. \sum \middle| a_{n} \right|$$ diverges.</paragraph>
        <paragraph>It converges absolutely.</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
