      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="53" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Suppose the series $$\Sigma a_{n}$$ is conditionally convergent.</paragraph>
        <list type="ordered">
          <item>Prove that the series $$\Sigma n^{2}a_{n}$$ is divergent.</item>
          <item>Conditional convergence of $$\Sigma a_{n}$$ is not enough to determine whether $$\Sigma na_{n}$$ is convergent. Show this by giving an example of a conditionally convergent series such that $$\Sigma na_{n}$$ converges and an example where $$\sum na_{n}$$ diverges.</item>
        </list>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$\sum\limits_{n = 2}^{\infty}\frac{\left( {- 1} \right)^{n}}{n\ln n}$$ ; $$\sum\limits_{n = 1}^{\infty}\frac{\left( {- 1} \right)^{n - 1}}{n}$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
